# Wi-Fi and Bluetooth firmware - xxri-firmware-wireless.tcz
# (rules/xxri-firmware-wireless.make)
#
# Source: linux-firmware 20260810 (pinned in rules/pre/xxri.make), through its
# WHENCE by scripts/xxri-fw-select.py.  The same extension carries
# regulatory.db from wireless-regdb (a second part of the rule).
#
# The drivers themselves are Tiny Core's (wireless- and bluetooth-6.12.11-
# tinycore.tcz).  Starting point: the names each module declares
# (scripts/xxri-fw-requested.sh <module> <tcz>).  Where a driver walks down
# from its newest firmware API (iwlwifi, ath10k), the list names the newest
# file this release has within the driver's range - e.g. iwlwifi asks for
# iwlwifi-6000-6, the release has -4, and the driver falls back to it.
#
# Scope: the Wi-Fi of machines and adapters up to about 2018, i.e. 802.11
# a/b/g/n and 802.11ac (Wi-Fi 5), on PCI, PCIe, CardBus and USB, and the
# Bluetooth part of the same combo cards and dongles.
#
# Left out, and what those devices do without it:
#   Wi-Fi 6/6E/7 - Intel AX2xx/BE2xx, Realtek RTL8851/8852/8922, MediaTek
#     MT7921/7922/7925/7915/7996, Qualcomm ath11k/ath12k: the driver loads
#     and fails to start the radio.  ~22 MB more.
#   Intel Wi-Fi 5 CNVi parts on Ice Lake/Comet Lake/Jasper Lake/Alder Lake
#     platforms (iwlwifi-Qu*/so-*-jf-b0, 1.9 MB): no Wi-Fi on those
#     machines; the 9560 on Coffee/Whiskey Lake and Gemini Lake is covered.
#   SDIO and board-specific parts (ath6kl, brcmfmac SDIO, wl12xx/wl18xx,
#     wilc1000, mwifiex/btmrvl SDIO, rtw88 SDIO): need per-board
#     calibration files linux-firmware does not have.
#   Broadcom brcmfmac PCIe (BCM4350, 43602) and BCM43569/4373 USB (1.3 MB).
#   ath10k QCA9887 and QCA6174 hw2.1 (early silicon), 60 GHz wil6210.
#   Not in linux-firmware at all: b43 for LP-PHY/N-PHY cores (BCM4312,
#     BCM4321/4322, BCM43227/43228) and b43legacy - Broadcom's licence
#     forbids redistribution; Prism54 USB/PCI (p54), Atmel at76c50x USB,
#     3Com/BlueFRITZ/BCM2033 Bluetooth.  Broadcom Bluetooth patch RAM
#     (BCM*.hcd) is not in linux-firmware either; btbcm then runs the
#     adapter on its ROM firmware, which works for ordinary use.
#
# Shipped from Tiny Core's packages instead (config/cde/manifest), because
# linux-firmware does not carry them: ipw2100/ipw2200 (Intel's own
# redistribution licence), zd1211 (GPL) and openfwwf, the open b43 firmware
# for 802.11g Broadcom cores (BCM4306 rev 3, BCM4311, BCM4318).
#
# No firmware needed: ath5k, ath9k (AR5xxx, AR92xx/93xx/94xx/95xx PCI/PCIe),
# rtl8180/rtl8187, rt2400pci/rt2500pci/rt2500usb, adm8211.

# -- Intel ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2005-2012, 802.11a/b/g/n (iwlegacy, iwldvm)
#   PRO/Wireless 3945ABG/BG
